index a059fe2..f27d00e 100644
--- a/docs/validation.md
+++ b/docs/validation.md
@@ -120,3 +120,57 @@ If even more customization is required, {func}`cattrs.transform_error` can be co
 
 Non-detailed validation can be enabled by initializing any of the converters with `detailed_validation=False`.
 In this mode, any errors during un/structuring will bubble up directly as soon as they happen.
+
+## Partial Structuring
+
+```{versionadded} 25.4.0
+
+```
+
+When processing untrusted input, it's sometimes useful to structure as much of the input as possible instead of just raising an exception.
+{meth}`BaseConverter.partial_structure <cattrs.BaseConverter.partial_structure>` (and the matching top-level function, {func}`cattrs.partial_structure`) does this; instead of raising, it returns a {class}`cattrs.PartialResult` describing what could and could not be structured.
+
+```python
+>>> from attrs import define
+>>> from cattrs import Converter
+
+>>> @define
+... class Person:
+...     name: str
+...     age: int = 0
+
+>>> converter = Converter()
+>>> res = converter.partial_structure({"name": "Jane", "age": "not a number"}, Person)
+>>> res.value
+Person(name='Jane', age=0)
+>>> res.is_complete
+False
+>>> sorted(res.structured_fields)
+['name']
+>>> sorted(res.failed_fields)
+['age']
+```
+
+The rules of partial structuring are:
+
+* Fields missing from the input are considered failed.
+* Failed fields with defaults fall back to these defaults; failed fields without defaults prevent a value from being produced, so {attr}`PartialResult.value <cattrs.PartialResult.value>` is `None`.
+* Nested _attrs_ classes, dataclasses and TypedDicts are partially structured recursively.
+  If a nested class can only be partially structured, its partial value is used and the containing field is marked as failed.
+* Collections (such as lists and dictionaries) are structured atomically; a single failing element fails the entire field.
+* Fields with `init=False` cannot be structured from mappings, so they are excluded from `structured_fields` and `failed_fields`.
+* When `forbid_extra_keys` is enabled, extra keys make the result incomplete, but a value is still produced.
+
+The failures themselves are available in the `error_map` (a mapping of field names to exceptions) and, aggregated, in `errors` (an ExceptionGroup when detailed validation is enabled).
+
+Failed fields can be fixed up using {meth}`PartialResult.refine <cattrs.PartialResult.refine>`, which returns a new {class}`cattrs.PartialResult`; successfully structured fields are preserved and cannot be overwritten.
+
+```python
+>>> fixed = res.refine({"age": 42})
+>>> fixed.value
+Person(name='Jane', age=42)
+>>> fixed.is_complete
+True
+```
+
+Since it works field-by-field using hooks instead of generated code, partial structuring is significantly slower than normal structuring.
